## Why This Is Asked

This question probes an advanced testing scenario where data consistency is eventual and involves a read-model updated by a streaming pipeline, requiring tests around read-your-writes, consistency window, multi-tenant isolation, and resilience to streaming outages.

## Key Concepts

- Eventual consistency between read-model and stream
- Read-your-writes and drift windows
- Per-tenant isolation under concurrency
- Streaming fault injection and recovery
- Contract testing across gateway and downstream services

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test sketch: verify eventual consistency
async function testReadYourWrites(tenantId, value){
  await writeMetric(tenantId, value);
  await untilTrue(async ()=> {
     const v = await readMetrics(tenantId);
     return v.includes(value);
  }, 30000);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure the real-world consistency window, and what metrics would you collect?
- How would you design roll-out and rollback strategies if drift exceeds SLA?

